Lab 5: Managing VM Lifecycles
Objectives
By the end of this lab, students will be able to:

Execute VM lifecycle operations using oc and virtctl command-line tools
Manage virtual machines through the OpenShift web console interface
Configure and implement VM run policies including AlwaysRun and Manual
Understand the different VM states and transitions in OpenShift Virtualization
Troubleshoot common VM lifecycle management issues
Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, students should have:

Basic understanding of OpenShift concepts and terminology
Familiarity with command-line interface operations
Knowledge of YAML configuration files
Completion of previous OpenShift Virtualization labs or equivalent experience
Access to an OpenShift cluster with OpenShift Virtualization operator installed
