Task 3: Configure VM Run Policies
Subtask 3.1: Understanding Run Policies
Learn about different VM run policies and their applications.

Run Policy Types:

Manual: VM starts/stops only through explicit user actions
Always: VM automatically restarts if it stops unexpectedly
RerunOnFailure: VM restarts only if it fails (exit code != 0)
Halted: VM remains stopped regardless of configuration
Subtask 3.2: Set AlwaysRun Policy via Command Line
Configure a VM to automatically restart using the AlwaysRun policy.

Create VM with AlwaysRun policy:
cat > always-run-vm.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: kubevirt.io/v1
kind: VirtualMachine
metadata:
  name: always-run-vm
  namespace: vm-lifecycle-lab
spec:
  runStrategy: Always
  template:
    metadata:
      labels:
        kubevirt.io/vm: always-run-vm
    spec:
      domain:
        cpu:
          cores: 1
        devices:
          disks:
          - disk:
              bus: virtio
            name: containerdisk
          - disk:
              bus: virtio
            name: cloudinitdisk
          interfaces:
          - masquerade: {}
            name: default
        machine:
          type: pc-q35-rhel8.4.0
        resources:
          requests:
            memory: 1Gi
      networks:
      - name: default
        pod: {}
      volumes:
      - containerDisk:
          image: quay.io/kubevirt/cirros-container-disk-demo
        name: containerdisk
      - cloudInitNoCloud:
          userData: |
            #cloud-config
            password: fedora
            chpasswd: { expire: False }
        name: cloudinitdisk
EOF
Apply the AlwaysRun VM:
oc apply -f always-run-vm.yaml
Verify the VM starts automatically:
oc get vm always-run-vm -n vm-lifecycle-lab
oc get vmi always-run-vm -n vm-lifecycle-lab
Subtask 3.3: Test AlwaysRun Policy Behavior
Verify that the AlwaysRun policy automatically restarts the VM.

Force stop the VM instance:
oc delete vmi always-run-vm -n vm-lifecycle-lab
Watch VM automatically restart:
watch "oc get vm always-run-vm -n vm-lifecycle-lab && echo '---' && oc get vmi always-run-vm -n vm-lifecycle-lab"
# Press Ctrl+C to exit watch
Verify automatic restart occurred:
oc get events -n vm-lifecycle-lab --field-selector involvedObject.name=always-run-vm
Subtask 3.4: Modify Run Policies
Practice changing run policies on existing VMs.

Change existing VM to Manual policy:
oc patch vm test-vm -n vm-lifecycle-lab --type merge -p '{"spec":{"runStrategy":"Manual","running":null}}'
Verify policy change:
oc get vm test-vm -n vm-lifecycle-lab -o yaml | grep -A5 -B5 runStrategy
Change to RerunOnFailure policy:
