Subtask 4.2: VM Snapshot Operations
Create and manage VM snapshots for backup and recovery.

Create a VM snapshot:
cat > vm-snapshot.yaml << EOF
apiVersion: snapshot.kubevirt.io/v1alpha1
kind: VirtualMachineSnapshot
metadata:
  name: test-vm-snapshot
  namespace: vm-lifecycle-lab
spec:
  source:
    apiVersion: kubevirt.io/v1
    kind: VirtualMachine
    name: test-vm
EOF
Apply snapshot configuration:
oc apply -f vm-snapshot.yaml
Check snapshot status:
oc get vmsnapshot -n vm-lifecycle-lab
Troubleshooting Common Issues
Issue 1: VM Fails to Start
Symptoms: VM remains in Starting state or shows error status

Solutions:

Check resource availability:
oc describe vm <vm-name> -n <namespace>
oc get events -n <namespace>
Verify node resources:
oc describe nodes
Check storage class availability:
oc get storageclass
Issue 2: virtctl Commands Not Working
Symptoms: Command not found or connection errors

Solutions:

Verify virtctl installation:
which virtctl
virtctl version
Check cluster connectivity:
oc whoami
oc cluster-info
Issue 3: Run Policy Not Taking Effect
Symptoms: VM doesn't restart automatically with Always policy

Solutions:

Verify policy configuration:
oc get vm <vm-name> -o yaml | grep -A5 -B5 runStrategy
Check for conflicting settings:
oc get vm <vm-name> -o yaml | grep running
Remove conflicting running field:
oc patch vm <vm-name> --type json -p '[{"op": "remove", "path": "/spec/running"}]'
